            <ArticleTitle>The nurse's role in pain relief.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>94-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite advances in the management of pain, undertreatment of pain continues to be a common problem in medical-surgical patients. Nurses are encouraged to learn more effective ways to control patients' pain and to accept accountability for pain control. To be effective patient advocates, nurses must be &quot;pain&quot; advocates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
